---
// "CILS, CELI, PLIDA or CERT.IT?": which certificate fits which purpose (content-plan §2). The
// page was moved here from /exams/dele-or-siele by `exams-plida-certit` (content-plan §2: new
// route /exams/which-exam). General orientation, every fact dated and "to verify": no prices,
// timings or pass marks are asserted here. Text lives in public/i18n/en.json; the markup holds
// the same English as a fallback. Keys still carry their old names (delesiele.*): .dele = CILS,
// .siele = CELI where a key is per exam.
import ExamDisclaimer from "../../components/ExamDisclaimer.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import "../../styles/practice.css";
import "../../styles/pruefungen.css";

const purposes = [
  {
    key: "nationality",
    title: "Italian citizenship",
    answer: "Usually B1, from a recognised certifying body",
    text: "For citizenship by residence or by marriage, the usual language proof is a certificate at B1 or higher. CILS, CELI, PLIDA and CERT.IT are the certifying bodies usually named for this. The rules changed in 2025 and some applicants are exempt, for example with a school or university diploma from Italy, so check your own case on the Ministero dell'Interno citizenship portal or with your Prefettura.",
  },
  {
    key: "visa",
    title: "Long-term EU residence permit",
    answer: "Usually A2",
    text: "For the permesso di soggiorno UE per soggiornanti di lungo periodo, you usually have to show Italian at A2. A certificate at A2 or higher from a recognised body is normally accepted instead of the Italian test given by the Prefettura. Ask your Questura or Prefettura which certificates it takes and whether you are exempt. This page is general orientation, not legal advice.",
  },
  {
    key: "work",
    title: "Work",
    answer: "Depends on the employer",
    text: "Private employers often care more about your level than about which certificate it came from. Public jobs and regulated professions can have fixed rules: check the call for applications (bando) or the professional body. If you have a choice, compare the next session dates, because they differ by certificate and by centre.",
  },
  {
    key: "university",
    title: "University and study",
    answer: "Ask the university first",
    text: "Universities that teach in Italian usually want a certificate at B2 or higher, but each university and each degree sets its own rule. Some name certain certificates, some run their own test. Get the rule in writing from the admissions office (segreteria studenti) and ask how old your certificate may be.",
  },
  {
    key: "self",
    title: "For yourself",
    answer: "Your choice",
    text: "If you want a goal to work towards, any of the four gives you a level to aim for and a certificate if you reach it. Which one fits depends on how and when you want to sit the exam, so compare the formats on the official pages.",
  },
];

// The four bodies stay in the table head; what we can't state safely says "check the official page".
const bodies = ["CILS", "CELI", "PLIDA", "CERT.IT"];
const checkRows = [
  { key: "shape", label: "Format and parts", text: "Check the official page." },
  { key: "result", label: "Result and pass rule", text: "Check the official page." },
  { key: "valid", label: "How long it lasts", text: "Check the official page, and ask the office that will read it." },
  { key: "price", label: "Price", text: "Check the official page. Prices differ by centre and country." },
];
---
<Layout
  title="CILS, CELI, PLIDA or CERT.IT? Which Italian exam you need – icanspeak Italian"
  description="Which Italian certificate fits citizenship (usually B1), the long-term EU residence permit (usually A2), work or university? General orientation, to be checked against the official pages."
>
  <SiteNav active="pruefungen" />
  <main class="practice-main practice-main--wide">
    <a href="/exams" class="vp-back-link" data-i18n="fallen.back">Back to the exams</a>

    <div class="practice-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="delesiele.eyebrow">Choosing an exam</p>
      <h1 data-i18n="delesiele.title">CILS, CELI, PLIDA or CERT.IT?</h1>
      <p data-i18n="delesiele.lead">
        These four certificates of Italian as a foreign language are the ones offices and universities most often ask for. What decides between them is what you need the result for. For citizenship the level is usually B1, for the long-term EU residence permit usually A2. Which certificates the office accepts is for the office to say, so ask first.
      </p>
      <ExamDisclaimer />
    </div>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.purpose.title">What do you need it for?</h2>
      {/* Headed paragraphs, not a table: these answers are too long for narrow columns on a phone. */}
      {purposes.map((p) => (
        <>
          <h3 data-i18n={`delesiele.p.${p.key}.title`}>{p.title}</h3>
          <p><strong data-i18n={`delesiele.p.${p.key}.answer`}>{p.answer}</strong></p>
          <p data-i18n={`delesiele.p.${p.key}.text`}>{p.text}</p>
          {p.key === "nationality" && <p><a href="/nationality" data-i18n="nat.link.more">How Italian citizenship works, step by step</a></p>}
        </>
      ))}
      <p class="format-note" data-i18n="delesiele.purpose.note">
        General orientation, not legal advice. Rules change (the citizenship rules changed in 2025), so before you pay for an exam, check with the office that will read your result: the Ministero dell'Interno portal, your Prefettura or Questura, or your Comune.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.compare.title">The four certificates side by side</h2>
      <div class="format-table-wrap">
        <table class="format-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th>{bodies.map((b) => <th translate="no">{b}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" data-i18n="delesiele.r.who.label">Who is behind it</th>
              <td translate="no" data-i18n="delesiele.r.who.dele">Università per Stranieri di Siena</td>
              <td translate="no" data-i18n="delesiele.r.who.siele">Università per Stranieri di Perugia</td>
              <td translate="no">Società Dante Alighieri</td>
              <td translate="no">Università Roma Tre</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" data-i18n="delesiele.r.levels.label">Levels</th>
              <td colspan="4" data-i18n="delesiele.r.levels.dele">Each certificate has several levels, in general from A1 up to C2. Which levels and which editions exist: check the official page.</td>
            </tr>
            {checkRows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-i18n={`delesiele.r.${r.key}.label`}>{r.label}</th>
                <td colspan="4" data-i18n={`delesiele.r.${r.key}.dele`}>{r.text}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="format-note" data-i18n="delesiele.compare.note">
        Written in November 2026 and still to be checked against the official pages. Formats, results, validity and prices differ by certificate, level and country and change over time, so we don't list them here. Check the official page of the certificate you plan to take.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.tips.title">If you still can't decide</h2>
      <ul class="task-points">
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.1">You don't know your level yet: try a practice test first and register only for a level you can reach. A certificate at the wrong level can end in a fail.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.2">You need the result for an office: ask which certificates it accepts, at which level and how old they may be, before you book.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.3">You need a result soon: compare the next session dates on the official pages. They differ by certificate and by centre.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.4">You want the certificate to last: how long it is valid differs by certificate and by office, so check this before you choose.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.5">You mostly hear one regional Italian: listen to the official sample recordings and practise understanding other accents too.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.practice.title">Practise here</h2>
      <div class="mock-cta">
        <h3 data-i18n="delesiele.practice.dele.title">CILS</h3>
        <p data-i18n="delesiele.practice.dele.text">Format and practice tests for the levels on this site, in the style of the exam.</p>
        <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/dele" data-i18n="delesiele.practice.dele.cta">To the CILS page</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mock-cta">
        <h3 translate="no">CELI</h3>
        <p data-i18n="delesiele.practice.celi.text">Practice sets by level, in the style of the exam.</p>
        <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/siele/levels" data-i18n="delesiele.practice.celi.cta">To the CELI page</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mock-cta">
        <h3 data-i18n="delesiele.practice.siele.title">PLIDA</h3>
        <p data-i18n="delesiele.practice.siele.text">Format and a practice set, in the style of the exam.</p>
        <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/siele" data-i18n="delesiele.practice.siele.cta">To the PLIDA page</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mock-cta">
        <h3 translate="no">CERT.IT</h3>
        <p data-i18n="delesiele.practice.certit.text">Format and an A2 practice set, in the style of the exam.</p>
        <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/certit" data-i18n="delesiele.practice.certit.cta">To the CERT.IT page</a>
      </div>
      <p class="format-note" data-i18n="delesiele.practice.level.note">Our own sets: A1 test (CILS page), CILS A2–B2, CELI A2–B1, PLIDA B1 reading and writing, CERT.IT A2. No set exists yet for the other levels.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.sources.title">Where to check</h2>
      {/* Official sites: URLs to verify before launch. */}
      <ul class="task-points">
        <li><a href="https://cils.unistrasi.it/" rel="noopener" data-i18n="delesiele.sources.siele">CILS: official page (Università per Stranieri di Siena)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cvcl.it/" rel="noopener" data-i18n="delesiele.sources.recog">CELI: official page (Università per Stranieri di Perugia)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://plida.it/" rel="noopener" data-i18n="delesiele.sources.dele">PLIDA: official page (Società Dante Alighieri)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.certificazioneitaliano.uniroma3.it/" rel="noopener" data-i18n="delesiele.sources.certit">CERT.IT: official page (Università Roma Tre)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
